Listen...

26
00:03:44,605 --> 00:03:48,233
I'm... choosing my words
very carefully here.

27
00:03:49,610 --> 00:03:50,611
You need to get ready.

28
00:03:51,403 --> 00:03:52,905
Today's gonna be a good day.

29
00:03:52,988 --> 00:03:54,574
You can sleep when you
get to the White House.

30
00:03:54,657 --> 00:03:56,909
Or maybe not.

31
00:03:58,869 --> 00:04:01,163
Get yourself together,
Will. I'll see you in a bit.

32
00:04:10,673 --> 00:04:11,924
Are you ready...

33
00:04:18,889 --> 00:04:20,015
to catch me?

34
00:04:28,398 --> 00:04:31,276
Doug, LeAnn... do you have a moment?

35
00:04:43,122 --> 00:04:45,415
Reporting live from the Piedmont Hotel,

36
00:04:45,499 --> 00:04:47,627
the excitement is definitely...

37
00:04:47,710 --> 00:04:50,170
Better not let them see the
name on your credentials.

38
00:04:51,088 --> 00:04:52,923
Those folks out there
love their president.

39
00:04:53,883 --> 00:04:56,010
I love pound cake.

40
00:04:56,093 --> 00:04:58,095
Doesn't mean it's good for me.

41
00:04:58,178 --> 00:04:59,513
How are you doing, Seth?

42
00:05:01,181 --> 00:05:03,726
- You got some foundation right here.
- Oh, jeez.

43
00:05:05,519 --> 00:05:07,354
And we call it the news.

44
00:05:07,437 --> 00:05:09,607
I'm doing commentary.

45
00:05:09,690 --> 00:05:12,317
Which means eventually
someone gets to ask me

46
00:05:12,401 --> 00:05:15,320
