the president's loss.

47
00:05:15,404 --> 00:05:17,197
Or his win.

48
00:05:19,992 --> 00:05:21,619
I wish you the best, Seth.

49
00:05:22,536 --> 00:05:23,871
You'll land somewhere.

50
00:05:24,538 --> 00:05:25,623
You're that type.

51
00:05:27,249 --> 00:05:29,126
We're going to have
a great night tonight.

52
00:05:30,085 --> 00:05:31,545
You don't have to spin me.

53
00:05:32,546 --> 00:05:33,923
How shall I say this?

54
00:05:35,132 --> 00:05:39,094
When I was single, I always
picked the loser's party.

55
00:05:40,304 --> 00:05:42,723
I met the last Mrs. Hammerschmidt
drowning in tequila shots

56
00:05:42,807 --> 00:05:44,183
at the Bob Dole ballroom.

57
00:05:45,225 --> 00:05:48,103
And here I am... single again.

58
00:06:04,954 --> 00:06:07,081
- You're not in Texas anymore.
- Doug, please.

59
00:06:07,164 --> 00:06:08,540
- Please what?
- Don't think you know me.

60
00:06:08,623 --> 00:06:10,167
Look, I just want to be
sure that you're ready for...

61
00:06:10,250 --> 00:06:11,961
Macallan will do what he has to.

62
00:06:13,921 --> 00:06:15,380
I like to win.

63
00:06:15,464 --> 00:06:18,258
Trophies, medals, staring
contests. You name it.

64
00:06:18,342 --> 00:06:20,219
You understand that, you understand me.

65
00:06:27,351 --> 00:06:28,894
Hello, everyone.

66
00:06:30,187 --> 00:06:31,981
Well, it's still early.

67
00:06:32,064 --> 00:06:34,399
There's a lot more
election to be had today.

68
00:06:34,483 --> 00:06:36,681
And we just want to apologize that,

69
00:06:36,706 --> 00:06:38,052
because we have a
little more work to do,

70
00:06:38,112 --> 00:06:39,529
we're not gonna be able
to get over to the ballroom

71
00:06:39,613 --> 00:06:41,991
as early as we would like
to. But once we do get there,

72
00:06:42,074 --> 00:06:44,785
we are going to shake the hand
of each and every one of you,

73
00:06:44,869 --> 00:06:49,498
to thank you for all the extraordinary
work that you've done for us.

74
00:06:49,581 --> 00:06:52,001
That's right, a round of
applause all the way around.

75
00:06:54,962 --> 00:06:57,297
And we'll see you all at
the party a little later.

76
00:07:41,926 --> 00:07:43,052
Better?

77
00:07:43,135 --> 00:07:46,055
Yeah, a little.

78
00:07:47,597 --> 00:07:50,059
First time I've fucked a president.

79
00:07:50,142 --> 00:07:53,020
- Oh, don't say that.
- Marshall said...

80
00:07:53,938 --> 00:07:55,439
I'm not a president yet.

81
00:07:56,231 --> 00:07:57,316
Almost.

82
00:08:06,616 --> 00:08:08,786
I got to put on a suit.

83
00:08:08,869 --> 00:08:11,663
- People will be here soon.
- Will...

84
00:08:13,999 --> 00:08:15,793
can't you let yourself feel it?

85
00:08:26,178 --> 00:08:27,179
Almost.

86
00:08:33,602 --> 00:08:34,718
Ready when you are, sir.

87
00:08:34,743 --> 00:08:35,879
Put the governor on, please.

88
00:08:35,938 --> 00:08:37,772
- Hello.
- Mitch, this is the president.

89
00:08:37,857 --> 00:08:39,191
I understand you've been briefed.

90
00:08:39,274 --> 00:08:41,110
Oh, Mr. President...

91
00:08:41,193 --> 00:08:43,570
this is catching us
all off guard over here.

92
00:08:43,653 --> 00:08:45,990
State, local, we had no idea.

93
00:08:46,073 --> 00:08:47,074
I understand.

94
00:08:47,157 --> 00:08:49,326
I'm with the vice president,
the secretary of state Durant,

95
00:08:49,409 --> 00:08:52,872
and on the line with us is
Counterterrorism Director Green.

96
00:08:52,955 --> 00:08:55,457
Governor, sir, I'm sorry,
but we needed to act.

97
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:57,877
I contacted local law
enforcement directly.

98
00:08:57,960 --> 00:08:59,669
Well, it took a while to get to me.

99
00:08:59,753 --> 00:09:01,130
Mitch, the counterterrorism director

100
00:09:01,213 --> 00:09:03,632
will be sharing information that
we must keep amongst ourselves.

101
00:09:03,715 --> 00:09:07,761
We do not want to do anything
that affects today's voting.

102
00:09:07,845 --> 00:09:08,929
Forty-five minutes ago,

103
00:09:09,013 --> 00:09:11,974
we raided the home of
Muhammed Kalabi, sir.

104
00:09:12,057 --> 00:09:13,142
On Deaderick Ave.

105
00:09:13,225 --> 00:09:15,853
- Yes.
- It's near the Coliseum.

106
00:09:15,936 --> 00:09:17,733
The suspect was not in his apartment,

107
00:09:17,758 --> 00:09:20,498
but we did find bomb-making material.

108
00:09:22,609 --> 00:09:24,862
- Jesus, uh...
- Now, Mitch...

109
00:09:24,945 --> 00:09:27,281
the last thing we want
is for you to panic.

110
00:09:28,407 --> 00:09:30,626
You must know that you
have the full support

111
00:09:30,651 --> 00:09:32,185
of the federal government here.

112
00:09:32,244 --> 00:09:35,039
Um, it... well, what... what's next?

113
00:09:35,122 --> 00:09:38,458
We believe his target is
one of the voting centers.

114
00:09:38,542 --> 00:09:39,877
We know you have soldiers in place,

115
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:43,088
security measures and checkpoints.
Director Green is on his way to you.

116
00:09:43,172 --> 00:09:46,091
There will be a command center
out of the FBI office in Knoxville

117
00:09:46,175 --> 00:09:47,301
where we will coordinate.

118
00:09:47,384 --> 00:09:49,887
My family voted at the
Coliseum this morning.

119
00:09:49,970 --> 00:09:53,933
Mitch, listen to me. Whatever
you need, we will provide.

120
00:09:57,186 --> 00:09:58,853
How are the Ohio numbers?

121
00:09:58,938 --> 00:10:01,106
It's hard to gauge
with turnout this low.

122
00:10:01,190 --> 00:10:02,399
That was kind of the point.

123
00:10:02,482 --> 00:10:04,443
For the other side, not Democrats.

124
00:10:04,526 --> 00:10:07,029
The governor's worried.
Do you have any numbers?

125
00:10:07,112 --> 00:10:08,989
No, just what we gave you.

126
00:10:09,073 --> 00:10:11,018
I would think that the
president might have access

127
00:10:11,043 --> 00:10:12,850
to some numbers that we don't.

128
00:10:12,910 --> 00:10:14,286
When I get them, you'll get them.

129
00:10:15,037 --> 00:10:16,746
- We're worried.
- Hang in there.

130
00:10:16,830 --> 00:10:19,249
I'll touch base with you
after the three o'clock wave.

131
00:10:20,834 --> 00:10:23,170
If you could all just give me
a moment, please. Thank you.

132
00:10:24,046 --> 00:10:25,593
You better head over to the ballroom.

133
00:10:25,618 --> 00:10:27,406
One of us should make an appearance.

134
00:10:27,466 --> 00:10:29,259
Sir, the day has finally arrived.

135
00:10:29,343 --> 00:10:32,221
Yes, and let's see just
how long this day lasts.

136
00:10:36,433 --> 00:10:39,909
Imagine my surprise
when the NSA called me

137
00:10:39,934 --> 00:10:42,171
about Muhammed Kalabi just...

138
00:10:42,231 --> 00:10:43,898
moments before you did.

139
00:10:45,192 --> 00:10:46,944
Situation is still unfolding.

140
00:10:47,027 --> 00:10:48,528
On Election Day?

141
00:10:54,368 --> 00:10:55,577
Francis...

142
00:10:56,578 --> 00:10:58,663
it's been quite a
journey working with you.

143
00:11:02,417 --> 00:11:04,336
Kalabi slipped into the country,

144
00:11:04,419 --> 00:11:06,638
and he's planning a terrorist attack...

145
00:11:06,663 --> 00:11:09,793
against a voting center in Tennessee.

146
00:11:10,550 --> 00:11:12,844
And that is a terrifying proposition.

147
00:11:14,346 --> 00:11:16,205
Well, I may need you to
stay around the White House

148
00:11:16,230 --> 00:11:19,226
a bit longer, Cathy, until
this situation is resolved.

149
00:11:20,644 --> 00:11:22,377
Of course.

150
00:11:23,897 --> 00:11:25,357
I was only saying...

151
00:11:26,816 --> 00:11:28,110
it's been a good run.

152
00:11:41,373 --> 00:11:44,459
As if she could ever get under my skin.

153
00:11:44,543 --> 00:11:46,961
I don't need to get
to the party just yet.

154
00:11:47,046 --> 00:11:50,674
Sweaty palms, eager to
pay me their last respects.

155
00:11:50,757 --> 00:11:53,218
When what they really want
to do to show their respect

156
00:11:53,302 --> 00:11:56,721
is to empty their bullets in my
body, just to make sure that I'm dead.

157
00:11:59,558 --> 00:12:01,851
Patti, I'm so sorry to keep you waiting.

158
00:12:01,935 --> 00:12:03,240
Miss Harvey was just telling me

159
00:12:03,265 --> 00:12:04,545
that there's been a
change in the schedule.

160
00:12:04,604 --> 00:12:07,149
Yes, unfortunately, we're
in a bit of an emergency.

161
00:12:07,232 --> 00:12:10,069
Uh, but I hope it will be resolved soon.

162
00:12:10,152 --> 00:12:11,861
Tom, hello.

163
00:12:13,363 --> 00:12:16,325
- You know Mr. Yates, don't you?
- Yes, we met at the convention.

164
00:12:16,408 --> 00:12:18,034
So LeAnn will be at the hotel.

165
00:12:18,125 --> 00:12:19,985
She can reach me if you
feel I need to be there

166
00:12:20,010 --> 00:12:22,367
sooner rather than later.

167
00:12:23,248 --> 00:12:25,959
Uh, in case it's later...

168
00:12:26,042 --> 00:12:28,170
I want you to think
four years down the road.

169
00:12:29,088 --> 00:12:31,047
- I'm sorry?
- They trust you.

170
00:12:32,757 --> 00:12:35,760
Four years is no time.

171
00:12:37,304 --> 00:12:38,680
We have a car waiting.

172
00:12:52,819 --> 00:12:54,654
So we're shaking hands today?

173
00:12:54,738 --> 00:12:56,865
I think it's best we keep it like that.

174
00:13:00,494 --> 00:13:01,995
Well, shake it like you mean it.

175
00:13:12,381 --> 00:13:13,423
How's that?

176
00:13:20,805 --> 00:13:23,392
So you want me to just
head over to the ballroom?

177
00:13:26,102 --> 00:13:27,103
No.

178
00:13:28,188 --> 00:13:29,189
No.

179
00:13:30,315 --> 00:13:32,776
I do like looking at
you across a large room.

180
00:13:41,451 --> 00:13:42,452
Victory.

181
00:13:46,248 --> 00:13:47,957
This is for when you win.

182
00:13:53,922 --> 00:13:55,840
I wrote a concession speech as well.

183
00:14:16,861 --> 00:14:18,853
With increased security
at polling places

184
00:14:18,878 --> 00:14:20,097
across the country,

185
00:14:20,157 --> 00:14:23,076
will fewer Americans vote
for the president this year

186
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:25,162
than in any election in recent memory?

187
00:14:25,245 --> 00:14:28,373
Particular attention is being paid
to typical battleground states,

188
00:14:28,457 --> 00:14:30,167
Ohio and Pennsylvania,

189
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:32,627
where voter turnout has
become a central issue

190
00:14:32,711 --> 00:14:35,422
that could make all the difference
in this historic election.

191
00:14:35,505 --> 00:14:38,967
You know, if turnout is
low in Philadelphia...

192
00:14:39,050 --> 00:14:40,802
the Underwoods are going under.

193
00:14:40,885 --> 00:14:43,430
You need a better in than that.

194
00:14:45,139 --> 00:14:48,518
You look like you've been chewed
up and shit out twice today.

195
00:14:48,602 --> 00:14:50,641
Seems like you're
having trouble focusing.

196
00:14:50,666 --> 00:14:52,437
You ever see a doctor about that?

197
00:14:52,772 --> 00:14:54,358
Um, what?

198
00:14:54,441 --> 00:14:56,401
Oh, 'cause I feel pretty
comfortable diagnosing you

199
00:14:56,485 --> 00:14:59,488
with too much on your fucking mind.

200
00:14:59,571 --> 00:15:02,532
Hey, let me get you something
real. I'm celebrating.

201
00:15:04,117 --> 00:15:05,202
Two Oban.

202
00:15:06,995 --> 00:15:08,205
Celebrating what?

203
00:15:08,288 --> 00:15:11,291
Oh, you know Tom
Hammerschmidt's long lead team?

204
00:15:12,626 --> 00:15:14,085
You're looking at the newest member.

205
00:15:14,711 --> 00:15:16,463
That guy never gives up.

206
00:15:16,546 --> 00:15:20,425
Mmm. I tell you what he's up
to, feed him things from you.

207
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:25,430
Don't you think it's a
little late for quid pro quo?

208
00:15:25,514 --> 00:15:27,599
Oh, the Underwoods could still win.

209
00:15:28,725 --> 00:15:29,851
We'll see.

210
00:15:31,019 --> 00:15:33,938
Either way, you still
have a couple more months.

211
00:15:36,233 --> 00:15:37,234
Yeah.

212
00:15:37,317 --> 00:15:39,027
I'll land somewhere.

213
00:15:42,071 --> 00:15:44,949
Your phone.

214
00:15:46,701 --> 00:15:49,037
Can somebody give me a
second today, you know?

215
00:15:49,954 --> 00:15:52,040
Shit. Excuse me.

216
00:15:52,957 --> 00:15:54,376
Hello?

217
00:15:54,459 --> 00:15:56,127
... While reports are coming in

218
00:15:56,210 --> 00:15:59,839
of a possible attack at
a Knoxville voting center.

219
00:15:59,923 --> 00:16:01,300
Now, let's take a live look...

220
00:16:01,383 --> 00:16:04,052
Tennessee? What's going on in Tennessee?

221
00:16:04,135 --> 00:16:06,095
... It's a very chaotic
scene at the moment.

222
00:16:06,179 --> 00:16:07,180
What?

223
00:16:07,264 --> 00:16:09,098
... There's a lot happening right now.

224
00:16:09,182 --> 00:16:10,643
Police are... are, of course,

225
00:16:10,668 --> 00:16:13,168
trying to keep everyone
calm and safe here.

226
00:16:13,193 --> 00:16:14,799
And we will bring you...

227
00:16:16,523 --> 00:16:18,024
Where the hell were you?

228
00:16:18,107 --> 00:16:19,901
Tennessee. What the hell's
going on in Tennessee?

229
00:16:19,984 --> 00:16:22,904
Muhammed Kalabi, the ICO guy
from Syria who burned the effigy.

230
00:16:22,987 --> 00:16:24,030
What's the plan?

231
00:16:24,113 --> 00:16:27,826
I stand before you this evening
as vice presidential candidate,

232
00:16:27,909 --> 00:16:30,161
as the First Lady of the United States,

233
00:16:30,244 --> 00:16:34,207
and most of all... as a
citizen of this great country.

234
00:16:35,041 --> 00:16:39,338
Despite the violent incident at
the voting center in Knoxville,

235
00:16:39,421 --> 00:16:42,341
which the president is
attending to as we speak,

236
00:16:42,424 --> 00:16:46,303
we want to assure anyone
who's considering not voting

237
00:16:46,386 --> 00:16:50,432
that it is not only safe to
vote, it is your duty to do so.

238
00:16:50,515 --> 00:16:52,812
It doesn't matter if you're a Democrat.

239
00:16:52,837 --> 00:16:54,627
It doesn't matter if
you're a Republican.

240
00:16:54,686 --> 00:16:57,314
Our nation needs you to vote today.

241
00:16:57,397 --> 00:16:59,649
Violence cannot beget apathy.

242
00:16:59,733 --> 00:17:02,569
We must make our voices heard.

243
00:17:03,487 --> 00:17:05,530
Seth!

244
00:17:05,614 --> 00:17:08,074
Witnesses report an FBI
and Homeland presence

245
00:17:08,157 --> 00:17:09,868
at the Knoxville voting center.

246
00:17:09,951 --> 00:17:11,411
Do you believe this is ICO-related?

247
00:17:11,495 --> 00:17:12,496
Seth, please! Come on.

248
00:17:12,579 --> 00:17:14,956
- And the FBI isn't talking.
- Neither are you, Gina.

249
00:17:15,039 --> 00:17:16,916
This isn't a presser,
because I didn't schedule one.

250
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,918
- We're just trying to find out...
- That's two, Gina.

251
00:17:19,002 --> 00:17:21,796
If you're looking for a
strikeout, I'm happy to oblige.

252
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:23,757
No? Good.

253
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:25,980
There's no questions at this time.

254
00:17:26,005 --> 00:17:27,576
The First Lady's statement stands as is.

255
00:17:27,636 --> 00:17:30,179
I will have updates for you
on Tennessee as I get them.

256
00:17:30,263 --> 00:17:32,015
Is everyone clear? Thank you.

257
00:17:32,098 --> 00:17:33,600
Seth!

258
00:17:41,107 --> 00:17:42,692
I'm told everything just went wrong.

259
00:17:42,776 --> 00:17:44,528
- The FBI had the bomb guys there...
- But, Mitch...

260
00:17:44,611 --> 00:17:45,862
... for crying out loud!

261
00:17:45,945 --> 00:17:47,614
... injuries didn't go
beyond scrapes and bruises.

262
00:17:47,697 --> 00:17:50,283
Oh, I don't know about that, Shawna.

263
00:17:50,367 --> 00:17:52,369
Twelve people were
taken to the hospital.

264
00:17:55,288 --> 00:17:57,902
Look, is there any
status on Green's ETA?

265
00:17:57,927 --> 00:17:59,459
- Secretary Stewart and I...
- Yes. Just a moment, sir.

266
00:17:59,543 --> 00:18:01,004
... cannot make a
determination without...

267
00:18:01,029 --> 00:18:03,917
- You need to take this.
- What? What?

268
00:18:04,756 --> 00:18:06,007
What the hell is this?

269
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:10,261
Hello.

270
00:18:10,344 --> 00:18:12,681
Governor. Mark Usher here.

271
00:18:12,764 --> 00:18:14,683
I think we met at the
conference in Sun Valley.

272
00:18:14,766 --> 00:18:15,934
Yes, that's right.

273
00:18:16,017 --> 00:18:18,437
Well, I wish I were calling
under better circumstances.

274
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:20,772
I wanted to know what
you're going to need.

275
00:18:20,855 --> 00:18:23,232
I can get some excellent people
down there fast in case you...

276
00:18:23,316 --> 00:18:25,777
you're feeling like you
need the extra security or...

277
00:18:25,860 --> 00:18:26,986
You there?

278
00:18:27,070 --> 00:18:28,488
I'm right here, yeah.

279
00:18:28,572 --> 00:18:30,031
I spoke to Shawna a few minutes ago,

280
00:18:30,114 --> 00:18:33,326
and we agreed that we absolutely
cannot disrupt this election.

281
00:18:33,410 --> 00:18:35,412
You called my secretary of state?

282
00:18:35,495 --> 00:18:37,038
Well, she called me.

283
00:18:37,121 --> 00:18:40,166
She is a leader of the party
in Tennessee. As are you.

284
00:18:43,503 --> 00:18:46,673
Do I need to remind you, sir,
that yours is a red state,

285
00:18:46,756 --> 00:18:48,425
and every Republican in
it is counting on you?

286
00:18:48,508 --> 00:18:50,969
- Thank you, Mr. Usher.
- Now, hold on.

287
00:18:51,052 --> 00:18:53,262
Shawna just wanted to ask what
can be done and what can't be done.

288
00:18:53,346 --> 00:18:56,140
She's like the rest of us,
trying to figure this thing out.

289
00:18:59,478 --> 00:19:01,270
Because of the scale
of a possible threat

290
00:19:01,354 --> 00:19:03,231
which we're still trying to determine,

291
00:19:03,314 --> 00:19:06,818
and because of the importance
of these, uh, voting centers,

292
00:19:06,901 --> 00:19:08,612
we're asking the governor to declare

293
00:19:08,695 --> 00:19:10,822
- a state of emergency...
- Will, could you please sit?

294
00:19:11,740 --> 00:19:13,074
I don't like it.

295
00:19:13,157 --> 00:19:16,285
Three o'clock wave said Tennessee's
locked up, no matter what.

296
00:19:18,121 --> 00:19:19,413
Love, no one can see.

297
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,126
What the hell?

298
00:19:24,898 --> 00:19:26,873
... Be potentially disturbing.

299
00:19:29,599 --> 00:19:32,301
They don't bark when there's a bomb.

300
00:19:32,385 --> 00:19:33,928
What do you mean, "They don't bark"?

301
00:19:34,012 --> 00:19:37,641
The canine units don't bark when
there's a bomb, Mr. President.

302
00:19:37,724 --> 00:19:39,308
Yeah, but the whole building heard it.

303
00:19:39,392 --> 00:19:41,728
They're trained to sit down
when they detect a bomb.

304
00:19:41,811 --> 00:19:43,813
- So did they sit down?
- No.

305
00:19:43,897 --> 00:19:45,273
Then there was no bomb.

306
00:19:45,356 --> 00:19:47,191
We think the barking was provoked.

307
00:19:47,275 --> 00:19:48,985
Provoked? Director
Green, that'll be enough.

308
00:19:49,068 --> 00:19:51,613
These dogs are our last
line of defense, sir.

309
00:19:51,696 --> 00:19:54,157
I think ICO got in there today.

310
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:55,867
And thank God they
didn't get a bomb off,

311
00:19:55,950 --> 00:19:58,411
but whatever operative they
got in there, I think...

312
00:19:58,436 --> 00:19:59,937
was used to provoke the riot.

313
00:19:59,996 --> 00:20:01,080
I said that is enough.

314
00:20:01,164 --> 00:20:02,874
You think ICO got all
the way in that building

315
00:20:02,957 --> 00:20:05,669
and then just decided
not to set off a bomb?

316
00:20:05,752 --> 00:20:06,815
Well, there are...

317
00:20:06,840 --> 00:20:08,392
We are not going to disrupt the voting.

318
00:20:08,417 --> 00:20:09,881
Mitch, would you please
talk some sense into him?

319
00:20:09,964 --> 00:20:11,424
- I...
- If we don't suspend,

320
00:20:11,508 --> 00:20:14,218
the Bureau cannot guarantee
the safety of these centers.

321
00:20:14,302 --> 00:20:16,596
Unacceptable. Find Kalabi.

322
00:20:16,695 --> 00:20:19,289
The governor does not wanna
have to institute a curfew

323
00:20:19,314 --> 00:20:20,647
this late in the game.

324
00:20:20,672 --> 00:20:22,894
- And, Mitch...
- Uh, yes, sir.

325
00:20:22,977 --> 00:20:25,992
... you are not closing the polls.

326
00:20:37,742 --> 00:20:38,827
You think we should?

327
00:20:40,328 --> 00:20:41,996
I can't weigh in on this.

328
00:21:02,225 --> 00:21:03,768
I need to talk to Shawna.

329
00:21:06,980 --> 00:21:08,323
How many scandals...

330
00:21:08,348 --> 00:21:11,359
should the public be expected to
endure before they say, "Enough"?

331
00:21:11,442 --> 00:21:13,653
Before they say, "I'm staying home"?

332
00:21:13,737 --> 00:21:16,948
Before they lose complete faith
in this democratic republic?

333
00:21:17,031 --> 00:21:19,609
This is a trend that
dates back at least...

334
00:21:19,634 --> 00:21:21,810
to when Nixon avoided jail time.

335
00:21:21,870 --> 00:21:24,080
Okay, we're out.

336
00:21:31,212 --> 00:21:33,590
- You're good.
- I don't need fans, Sean.

337
00:21:33,673 --> 00:21:35,884
Just genuine appreciation.

338
00:21:35,967 --> 00:21:38,803
Would you like a drink?
One is brown and one is not.

339
00:21:38,887 --> 00:21:41,472
- It's gonna be a long night.
- That's not what I hear.

340
00:21:41,555 --> 00:21:43,432
So, Tennessee...

341
00:21:43,516 --> 00:21:44,558
Is the question.

342
00:21:44,643 --> 00:21:45,727
And?

343
00:21:45,810 --> 00:21:47,228
My date knew nothing.

344
00:21:47,311 --> 00:21:48,688
Are you making the rounds?

345
00:21:48,772 --> 00:21:50,899
Crowd's a little older
than I'm used to, but...

346
00:21:50,982 --> 00:21:54,944
yes, they're a talkative
bunch... that don't say much.

347
00:21:56,487 --> 00:21:57,739
I'll take the brown one.

348
00:21:59,658 --> 00:22:02,493
That's Patricia Whittaker over
there. Chairperson of the DNC.

349
00:22:02,576 --> 00:22:04,328
She slapped me once in a bar in Omaha.

350
00:22:04,412 --> 00:22:05,997
For the life of me,
I can't tell you why.

351
00:22:11,085 --> 00:22:12,879
There's something wrong with Tennessee.

352
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:15,840
Your date is either lying or denying.

353
00:22:37,987 --> 00:22:40,323
What did you mean by this?

354
00:22:41,825 --> 00:22:43,201
On the back of the speech?

355
00:22:46,329 --> 00:22:48,122
Nothing. Forget it.

356
00:22:50,959 --> 00:22:52,919
"There's still time"?

357
00:22:55,171 --> 00:22:56,589
There's still time for what?

358
00:23:00,301 --> 00:23:01,469
What are you doing?

359
00:23:02,929 --> 00:23:04,097
You and your husband.

360
00:23:05,139 --> 00:23:07,058
Getting ready to win an election.

361
00:23:08,434 --> 00:23:10,103
I see the way you're acting.

362
00:23:21,906 --> 00:23:25,994
Do you realize we have every
intention of winning today?

363
00:23:27,578 --> 00:23:28,621
Sure.

364
00:23:30,623 --> 00:23:31,791
But then what?

365
00:23:49,058 --> 00:23:52,228
I used to go to this
cabin... up in Maine.

366
00:23:54,730 --> 00:23:56,816
The windows don't close properly.

367
00:23:59,068 --> 00:24:02,363
You can smell the ocean all summer long.

368
00:24:19,463 --> 00:24:21,925
I do think it's better
you go to the ballroom.

369
00:24:35,313 --> 00:24:39,818
If you have not voted, I assure
you, you will get the chance.

370
00:24:39,901 --> 00:24:42,445
But I cannot, in good conscience,

371
00:24:42,528 --> 00:24:46,740
allow balloting to continue until
I am satisfied that it is safe.

372
00:24:46,825 --> 00:24:49,785
To that end, as nightfall approaches,

373
00:24:49,869 --> 00:24:55,083
I am announcing an enforced,
state-wide curfew, effective tonight.

374
00:24:55,166 --> 00:24:58,920
If you are not in your home
by 8:30 p.m. central time,

375
00:24:59,003 --> 00:25:02,673
or by 9:30 in the eastern
parts of this state,

376
00:25:02,756 --> 00:25:06,677
you will be subject to
detention and possible arrest.

377
00:25:06,760 --> 00:25:08,471
What the hell's going on?

378
00:25:08,554 --> 00:25:11,640
What's going on is we're gonna
win Pennsylvania and Ohio.

379
00:25:11,724 --> 00:25:13,351
That puts you over 270.

380
00:25:13,434 --> 00:25:15,353
The polls are still open.
People are still voting.

381
00:25:15,436 --> 00:25:19,107
My gut says they're ours.
That's 272 without Tennessee.

382
00:25:19,190 --> 00:25:21,025
That asshole's suspending the vote.

383
00:25:21,109 --> 00:25:23,777
That's up to his secretary of
state, and she's on our side.

384
00:25:23,862 --> 00:25:26,155
- She's gonna have a choice after this?
- Governor, listen to me.

385
00:25:26,239 --> 00:25:27,573
I mean, how long do we
let Francis Underwood

386
00:25:27,656 --> 00:25:29,617
get away with this kind
of shit? Huh? How long?

387
00:25:29,700 --> 00:25:31,119
He won't get away with it.

388
00:25:31,202 --> 00:25:32,328
He won't.

389
00:25:32,411 --> 00:25:34,038
That was Tennessee governor...

390
00:25:34,122 --> 00:25:35,999
Trust me.

391
00:25:36,082 --> 00:25:38,334
Bullshit.

392
00:25:40,086 --> 00:25:42,881
Voting centers all across
the state are being shut down,

393
00:25:42,964 --> 00:25:44,298
and anyone not in their homes

394
00:25:44,382 --> 00:25:47,385
by 8:30 central time, or 9:30...

395
00:25:47,468 --> 00:25:50,972
Five o'clock wave from
Philly. I think we're home.

396
00:25:51,055 --> 00:25:53,349
... Detention and possible
arrest. This announcement...

397
00:26:00,273 --> 00:26:02,066
That Tennessee shit is crazy.

398
00:26:03,692 --> 00:26:04,944
Crazy shit happens all the time.

399
00:26:05,736 --> 00:26:06,862
This convenient?

400
00:26:09,365 --> 00:26:11,534
Spare me the conspiracy talk.

401
00:26:11,617 --> 00:26:14,370
The government's not that
powerful... or competent.

402
00:26:17,081 --> 00:26:18,374
A man can ask.

403
00:26:24,964 --> 00:26:27,967
We're looking at 255
Underwood, 245 Conway.

404
00:26:28,051 --> 00:26:29,260
Pennsylvania and Ohio?

405
00:26:29,343 --> 00:26:31,470
Still too close, but
it's almost six o' clock.

406
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:35,099
When we change Tennessee
from Conway to undecided...

407
00:26:35,183 --> 00:26:36,948
- That brings Conway down to...
- Two thirty-four.

408
00:26:37,027 --> 00:26:38,064
Still way too close.

409
00:26:38,089 --> 00:26:40,479
Yes, but we don't yet know that
he's locked in the western states.

410
00:26:40,563 --> 00:26:42,148
Those states have been
locked up for ten years.

411
00:26:42,231 --> 00:26:45,484
Red, red, red and they'll be red
again by the end of the night.

412
00:26:45,568 --> 00:26:47,528
It's gonna come down to
Pennsylvania and Ohio.

413
00:26:47,611 --> 00:26:50,323
Conway needs both. You only need one.

414
00:26:50,406 --> 00:26:51,407
Matthews?

415
00:26:52,033 --> 00:26:54,743
He'll push back. He
might even go public.

416
00:26:54,827 --> 00:26:56,495
What about the other
five states in play?

417
00:26:56,579 --> 00:26:57,746
The lawyers are waiting.

418
00:26:57,830 --> 00:26:59,707
We can generate lawsuits,
argue suppression, but...

419
00:26:59,790 --> 00:27:00,959
Still not enough.

420
00:27:02,876 --> 00:27:05,171
Olmstead's losing in Ohio,
and he's not taking it well.

421
00:27:05,254 --> 00:27:07,298
I spoke with his chief of
staff, Tanya, this morning.

422
00:27:07,381 --> 00:27:09,425
He's getting clobbered in the
northern part of the state.

423
00:27:09,508 --> 00:27:12,053
Low turnout in Cleveland's not
helping. But he could still pull it out.

424
00:27:12,136 --> 00:27:14,472
He's not going to win and he knows it.

425
00:27:16,140 --> 00:27:17,391
How much time do we have?

426
00:27:17,475 --> 00:27:20,769
Ohio closes in two hours. And
most people voted this morning.

427
00:27:21,645 --> 00:27:23,147
Some of these states
are baked in already.

428
00:27:27,860 --> 00:27:29,403
Claire and I need the room for a moment.

429
00:27:30,321 --> 00:27:31,322
Yes, sir.

430
00:27:31,405 --> 00:27:33,782
- LeAnn, we'll call you back.
- Yes, sir.

431
00:27:45,128 --> 00:27:46,379
Why did you ask him to leave?

432
00:27:50,133 --> 00:27:54,637
Because I just wanted to look
in your eyes one more time

433
00:27:54,720 --> 00:27:56,597
before we do this.

434
00:27:58,932 --> 00:27:59,933
Francis...

435
00:28:00,518 --> 00:28:01,727
we're doing this.

436
00:28:10,153 --> 00:28:13,906
He can't save us. He
invented term limits.

437
00:28:16,450 --> 00:28:17,493
Doug!

438
00:28:19,703 --> 00:28:22,623
Get me LeAnn Harvey back on the phone.

439
00:28:22,706 --> 00:28:23,749
Yes, sir.

440
00:28:23,832 --> 00:28:25,751
Do what you have to do with Ohio.

441
00:28:25,834 --> 00:28:27,503
I'm on it.

442
00:28:28,504 --> 00:28:30,548
LeAnn, get the lawyers ready.

443
00:28:33,134 --> 00:28:35,136
- I can't do this.
- Yes, you can.

444
00:28:35,219 --> 00:28:38,389
- No, no, no, no, no!
- And it needs to be done quickly.

445
00:28:38,472 --> 00:28:40,266
It's too sloppy.

446
00:28:40,349 --> 00:28:42,101
Why are you here if LeAnn called me?

447
00:28:42,185 --> 00:28:43,880
Do I really have to explain
to you what will happen

448
00:28:43,905 --> 00:28:44,997
if you don't do this?

449
00:28:45,022 --> 00:28:47,565
I don't care if he loses.

450
00:28:47,648 --> 00:28:51,419
I'm not talking about the
election. I'm talking about you.

451
00:28:51,444 --> 00:28:53,779
What will happen to you?

452
00:28:56,115 --> 00:28:59,327
You have everything you need.
The Pastebin link was sent to you.

453
00:29:03,414 --> 00:29:04,415
Where's LeAnn?

454
00:29:04,498 --> 00:29:06,292
She's not here, and I'm short on time.

455
00:29:33,361 --> 00:29:36,364
Governor, I'm sorry, but there's
only one way to play this.

456
00:29:36,447 --> 00:29:38,033
We need you to pull your poll workers

457
00:29:38,058 --> 00:29:39,474
and your machines from
those three counties.

458
00:29:39,533 --> 00:29:41,619
The Republicans would crucify
me. They own that area.

459
00:29:41,702 --> 00:29:44,830
But those are the precincts that
are most likely to be threatened.

460
00:29:44,913 --> 00:29:47,040
"Likely to be"? Hey, what are you...

461
00:29:47,125 --> 00:29:48,959
What are we talking about here?

462
00:29:49,042 --> 00:29:50,128
Terrorist chatter.

463
00:29:50,211 --> 00:29:51,712
Related to Tennessee?

464
00:29:51,795 --> 00:29:53,046
Yes, sir.

465
00:29:53,131 --> 00:29:54,548
Well, I'm gonna need more
than your word on that.

466
00:29:54,632 --> 00:29:57,218
Oh, I'm sorry, but the intelligence
is classified, Governor.

467
00:29:57,301 --> 00:29:58,844
Then read me in.

468
00:29:58,927 --> 00:30:01,347
'Cause I'm not doing this
without seeing tangible proof

469
00:30:01,430 --> 00:30:02,931
with my own eyes. You can tell Francis.

470
00:30:03,015 --> 00:30:05,851
The other thing is,
with Ohio turnout so low,

471
00:30:05,934 --> 00:30:08,229
people could accuse you of
engaging in voter suppression.

472
00:30:08,312 --> 00:30:09,313
What?

473
00:30:09,397 --> 00:30:13,276
The voting centers and the
troops were the president's idea.

474
00:30:13,359 --> 00:30:16,237
But you signed on to them,
and that's what matters.

475
00:30:16,904 --> 00:30:19,782
You're losing your election,
sir. The signs are clear.

476
00:30:20,533 --> 00:30:23,161
That'd be a real shame for the
Democrats to be down a governor.

477
00:30:23,244 --> 00:30:26,122
But here we have this
confluence of events.

478
00:30:26,205 --> 00:30:30,209
Your disappointing returns on one
hand and the chatter on the other.

479
00:30:31,127 --> 00:30:33,796
I need proof. Otherwise,
people will think...

480
00:30:33,879 --> 00:30:36,632
That you shut down voting
in Republican precincts

481
00:30:36,715 --> 00:30:37,966
to guarantee your own win.

482
00:30:38,725 --> 00:30:39,990
Now I'd say it's a good thing

483
00:30:40,015 --> 00:30:43,045
that the NSA just picked
up on some credible chatter.

484
00:30:43,096 --> 00:30:44,807
This dangerous world left you no choice.

485
00:30:47,100 --> 00:30:49,437
Oh... thank you.

486
00:30:50,563 --> 00:30:54,024
Governor, I was just
handed the classified intel.

487
00:30:55,359 --> 00:30:56,735
Are you on a secure server?

488
00:30:56,819 --> 00:30:58,821
- Yes, I am.
- Please hold.

489
00:31:03,867 --> 00:31:05,661
I'm sending the files over right now.

490
00:31:21,093 --> 00:31:24,347
You're doing the right thing, sir.
We don't want blood on our hands.

491
00:31:27,015 --> 00:31:29,727
I don't care where they're
taking the voting machines.

492
00:31:29,810 --> 00:31:30,811
Just stay...

493
00:31:30,894 --> 00:31:33,689
You chain yourself to one
of them if you have to.

494
00:31:33,772 --> 00:31:35,649
Good. I'm gonna find an Ohio judge.

495
00:31:36,567 --> 00:31:39,487
Voting centers in Ohio have
been closed for almost two hours.

496
00:31:39,570 --> 00:31:41,780
And Conway's got a judge.
He's petitioning to reopen.

497
00:31:41,864 --> 00:31:44,575
But even if they stay closed,
would Ohio get us there?

498
00:31:44,658 --> 00:31:46,244
Other states might be in play.

499
00:31:46,327 --> 00:31:48,579
Rumblings of suppression
are out there, although...

500
00:31:48,662 --> 00:31:51,207
- Well, what else do we have?
- Voter intimidation in Idaho.

501
00:31:51,290 --> 00:31:53,251
What do you think? Should I call
them back and have them file?

502
00:31:54,001 --> 00:31:55,211
I like it.

503
00:31:55,294 --> 00:31:57,755
It has the most resonance with
what's happened in Tennessee.

504
00:31:57,838 --> 00:32:00,299
I also like an assemblyman
we have in Georgia.

505
00:32:00,383 --> 00:32:01,842
There's a congressman in Maryland.

506
00:32:01,925 --> 00:32:04,220
That's one of the states that
didn't request the troops.

507
00:32:04,303 --> 00:32:06,222
But wait. Don't we need
something coming from a voter?

508
00:32:06,305 --> 00:32:10,183
There's a voter in Mississippi.
Said she was too scared to vote.

509
00:32:10,268 --> 00:32:11,852
That TV essentially told her not to go.

510
00:32:11,935 --> 00:32:13,562
Well, that sounds like
a bit of a stretch.

511
00:32:13,646 --> 00:32:17,608
That could be a plus for us,
sir. Really open things up.

512
00:32:17,691 --> 00:32:20,653
If Ohio stays shut, there
could be a ripple effect.

513
00:32:20,736 --> 00:32:22,821
This is all uncharted territory.

514
00:32:22,905 --> 00:32:25,073
All right, let's put a pin
in Georgia and Maryland,

515
00:32:25,157 --> 00:32:27,660
and let's keep the Ohio
voting centers shut down,

516
00:32:27,743 --> 00:32:29,202
and see where that gets us.

517
00:32:29,287 --> 00:32:31,914
Pennsylvania has gone to Conway.

518
00:32:31,997 --> 00:32:34,708
Even if Ohio is still too close to call

519
00:32:34,792 --> 00:32:37,878
and the president does
well in the Northwest,

520
00:32:37,961 --> 00:32:40,631
he can't counter Conway's
gains in the South,

521
00:32:40,714 --> 00:32:43,008
in what would typically
be Underwood territory.

522
00:32:43,091 --> 00:32:44,718
The people have spoken.

523
00:32:46,011 --> 00:32:47,596
I can't believe this.

524
00:32:47,680 --> 00:32:50,349
The president apologizes that
he couldn't be here tonight,

525
00:32:50,433 --> 00:32:53,644
but he wanted me to let you know
that concession is inevitable.

526
00:32:55,103 --> 00:32:56,730
All the states haven't been called yet.

527
00:32:56,814 --> 00:32:58,482
The president still
has time if he needs...

528
00:32:58,566 --> 00:33:00,776
Guys, we fought a good fight.

529
00:33:00,859 --> 00:33:04,071
But, unfortunately, this is
the reality of the situation.

530
00:33:04,154 --> 00:33:06,657
Jesus.

531
00:33:07,658 --> 00:33:08,951
Well, I guess that's that.

532
00:33:13,121 --> 00:33:15,123
Yeah, this is Will.

533
00:33:15,207 --> 00:33:17,042
I wanted to be the first to tell you

534
00:33:17,125 --> 00:33:19,628
congratulations, Mr. President-elect.

535
00:33:21,088 --> 00:33:22,881
Well, thank you, Mr. President.

536
00:33:23,466 --> 00:33:25,759
Oh, what? You think I
learned nothing from Al Gore?

537
00:33:27,761 --> 00:33:29,597
We kept them on the edge
of their seats, didn't we?

538
00:33:31,932 --> 00:33:34,059
I guess that means
the system is working.

539
00:33:34,142 --> 00:33:35,811
I guess it does.

540
00:33:35,894 --> 00:33:38,021
You're about as tough an
opponent as they come, Francis.

541
00:33:38,105 --> 00:33:39,565
Well, I've had a lot of practice.

542
00:33:39,648 --> 00:33:42,985
Now, you be sure to give my
regards to Hannah and the children.

543
00:33:43,068 --> 00:33:44,778
Thank you, Mr. President. I'm...

544
00:33:45,696 --> 00:33:48,532
sure I'll be calling on you for
advice in the very near future.

545
00:33:48,616 --> 00:33:50,200
Well, I look forward to that.

546
00:34:01,337 --> 00:34:02,713
He conceded?

547
00:34:08,093 --> 00:34:09,970
Yeah.

548
00:34:12,806 --> 00:34:14,725
We did it.

549
00:34:16,977 --> 00:34:18,311
We did it.

550
00:34:19,355 --> 00:34:21,357
Excuse me, sir.

551
00:34:21,440 --> 00:34:23,401
General Brockhart is on
his way over to the suite.

552
00:34:23,484 --> 00:34:24,485
Thank you.

553
00:34:32,785 --> 00:34:34,912
Sources are telling us
that Francis Underwood

554
00:34:34,995 --> 00:34:36,372
conceded to Governor Conway

555
00:34:36,455 --> 00:34:38,957
on the phone only a short time ago.

556
00:34:39,041 --> 00:34:41,794
I suspect their numbers
are matching up with ours,

557
00:34:41,877 --> 00:34:44,588
which would put Ohio in
the Republican column.

558
00:34:44,672 --> 00:34:49,259
Enough to make William Conway the
next president of the United States.

559
00:34:57,726 --> 00:34:59,645
- Hello?
- Tanya, put him on the line.

560
00:34:59,728 --> 00:35:00,813
Hang on, let me see if I can get him.

561
00:35:00,896 --> 00:35:03,315
He's my secretary of state,
and he has the power to do it.

562
00:35:03,399 --> 00:35:04,983
Well, then you need
to tell him what to do.

563
00:35:05,067 --> 00:35:07,736
He says he can reopen and extend
the voting day into tomorrow.

564
00:35:07,820 --> 00:35:09,071
Tell him it's not safe.

565
00:35:09,154 --> 00:35:11,740
I've done that, Doug! Obviously,
he doesn't seem to care.

566
00:35:11,824 --> 00:35:13,534
Underwood conceded already.

567
00:35:13,617 --> 00:35:17,120
Do not trot out your secretary of state.

568
00:35:17,204 --> 00:35:18,371
Voting cannot resume.

569
00:35:18,456 --> 00:35:20,874
Now, if you have any doubt,
you swallow it right now.

570
00:35:20,958 --> 00:35:23,168
I'm worried about the party.
What this could do to the party.

571
00:35:23,251 --> 00:35:25,212
Roger, this is so much
bigger than the party.

572
00:35:26,547 --> 00:35:28,466
I feel like I'm risking
my entire career here.

573
00:35:28,549 --> 00:35:29,883
You are.

574
00:35:29,967 --> 00:35:33,429
And if you don't do what I'm
telling you, it's over for sure.

575
00:35:39,267 --> 00:35:40,268
What?

576
00:35:47,400 --> 00:35:49,166
How many hours is it gonna take him

577
00:35:49,191 --> 00:35:51,013
to spit out the fucking words in public?

578
00:35:51,071 --> 00:35:53,281
Hey, screw this. Screw
protocol. I'm heading down there.

579
00:35:53,365 --> 00:35:55,158
- No, you're not.
- It's already tomorrow, Mark.

580
00:35:55,242 --> 00:35:56,462
I mean, this is insane.

581
00:35:56,487 --> 00:35:59,162
- I want to make my speech!
- Ohio is still in play.

582
00:35:59,246 --> 00:36:00,288
What?

583
00:36:01,999 --> 00:36:03,626
What are you talking about?

584
00:36:03,709 --> 00:36:05,753
... Fear from continued
terrorist threats

585
00:36:05,836 --> 00:36:09,388
and the disturbing news
coming out of Tennessee...

586
00:36:10,841 --> 00:36:13,969
I was forced to close a
number of our polling places.

587
00:36:17,430 --> 00:36:19,725
Fuck me.

588
00:36:21,852 --> 00:36:24,437
And in accordance with the
Ohio secretary of state,

589
00:36:25,188 --> 00:36:27,399
the vote is suspended
until further notice.

590
00:36:31,529 --> 00:36:34,156
Now, I know this may put our
electorates in question...

591
00:36:35,616 --> 00:36:37,763
but I had no choice.

592
00:36:40,954 --> 00:36:44,708
New Jersey might not certify. There's
been a variety of irregularities.

593
00:36:44,792 --> 00:36:48,587
Same with Illinois. Looks like
Nevada's making noises, too.

594
00:36:51,549 --> 00:36:54,342
I'm having déjà vu. You ever get that?

595
00:36:57,012 --> 00:36:58,722
Are you seriously asking
me about déjà vu?

596
00:36:58,806 --> 00:37:01,058
Never mind. It's gone.

597
00:37:02,768 --> 00:37:05,478
You never get déjà vu? Everybody does.

598
00:37:05,563 --> 00:37:06,564
I don't.

599
00:37:08,148 --> 00:37:11,527
Don't look so worried, Doug. You
just felt familiar for a second.

600
00:37:12,611 --> 00:37:14,071
It's over.

601
00:37:14,154 --> 00:37:16,990
Now, the presidency
hangs in the balance.

602
00:37:17,074 --> 00:37:19,993
At least six states will not
have certified vote totals

603
00:37:20,077 --> 00:37:22,162
on Election Night 2016.

604
00:37:24,164 --> 00:37:25,332
Good evening.

605
00:37:26,542 --> 00:37:29,002
I guess I should say good morning. Um...

606
00:37:31,964 --> 00:37:34,382
Will wishes he could be here himself...

607
00:37:35,300 --> 00:37:37,636
but we've been advised
that goes against protocol.

608
00:37:39,096 --> 00:37:40,222
I know...

609
00:37:41,557 --> 00:37:42,933
you're disappointed.

610
00:37:44,226 --> 00:37:46,228
Are you okay with the word disappointed?

611
00:37:49,272 --> 00:37:51,316
Shouldn't we acknowledge their outrage?

612
00:37:51,399 --> 00:37:52,985
I'd say we should tread lightly.

613
00:37:53,068 --> 00:37:55,237
For now, we're just
asking for their patience.

614
00:37:55,320 --> 00:37:57,447
Okay, let's do it.

615
00:37:58,782 --> 00:38:01,326
Never a dull moment in this country.

616
00:38:02,703 --> 00:38:04,747
Will wishes he could be here himself,

617
00:38:04,830 --> 00:38:08,166
but we've been advised that
would go against protocol.

618
00:38:09,084 --> 00:38:13,421
I know you're disappointed that
the change you were hoping for...

619
00:38:13,505 --> 00:38:15,548
... that you voted for,

620
00:38:15,633 --> 00:38:17,509
has to wait a little longer.

621
00:38:35,402 --> 00:38:38,155
And, finally, a night
of electoral indecision,

622
00:38:38,238 --> 00:38:41,033
with lawsuits being filed
in nearly every state,

623
00:38:41,116 --> 00:38:43,452
has ended with the mayor of Honolulu,

624
00:38:43,477 --> 00:38:45,269
in the last state to close its polls,

625
00:38:45,328 --> 00:38:49,166
refusing to honor the results of
the election and filing a lawsuit.

626
00:38:49,875 --> 00:38:51,126
Was Hawaii one of ours?

627
00:38:51,209 --> 00:38:53,295
No, I don't think so.

628
00:38:56,214 --> 00:38:59,467
Claire, could you do me a little favor?

629
00:39:00,468 --> 00:39:04,139
I have a splitting headache. Could
you rub my temples for a moment?

630
00:39:05,307 --> 00:39:06,474
Of course.

631
00:39:10,395 --> 00:39:13,398
No, actually the pain
is right behind my eyes.

632
00:39:13,481 --> 00:39:16,902
Could you just... rub my eyes for me?

633
00:39:18,111 --> 00:39:19,988
But you hate that.

634
00:39:20,072 --> 00:39:22,407
I know, but I think
I'll like it this time.

635
00:39:33,919 --> 00:39:35,462
You can do it harder.

636
00:39:38,090 --> 00:39:40,383
Even harder than that.

637
00:39:54,022 --> 00:39:55,983
There's no coming back from this.

638
00:39:57,735 --> 00:40:00,278
Oh, I know exactly
what we're about to do.

639
00:40:01,363 --> 00:40:04,700
If we fail, it's on both of us.
I won't be able to protect you.

640
00:40:06,326 --> 00:40:08,871
And what a relief that will be...

641
00:40:10,080 --> 00:40:11,289
for both of us.

642
00:40:15,418 --> 00:40:18,881
The American people don't
know what's best for them.

643
00:40:18,964 --> 00:40:19,965
I do.

644
00:40:21,842 --> 00:40:24,136
I know exactly what they need.

645
00:40:25,804 --> 00:40:28,223
They're like little children, Claire.

646
00:40:29,141 --> 00:40:30,976
Children we never had.

647
00:40:32,227 --> 00:40:36,940
We have to hold their sticky
fingers and wipe their filthy mouths.

648
00:40:37,024 --> 00:40:39,067
Teach them right from wrong.

649
00:40:39,151 --> 00:40:42,195
Tell them what to think and
how to feel and what to want.

650
00:40:43,363 --> 00:40:46,491
They even need help writing
their wildest dreams,

651
00:40:46,574 --> 00:40:48,827
crafting their worst fears.

652
00:40:51,872 --> 00:40:53,248
Lucky for them...

653
00:40:54,833 --> 00:40:56,126
they have me...

654
00:40:57,961 --> 00:40:59,421
they have you.

655
00:41:02,257 --> 00:41:03,466
Underwood.

656
00:41:05,593 --> 00:41:06,804
Underwood.

657
00:41:08,055 --> 00:41:09,472
2016.

658
00:41:13,226 --> 00:41:14,477
2020.

659
00:41:18,148 --> 00:41:19,482
2024.

660
00:41:22,735 --> 00:41:23,946
2028.

661
00:41:25,948 --> 00:41:27,365
2032.

662
00:41:29,659 --> 00:41:31,536
2036.

663
00:41:35,373 --> 00:41:37,625
One nation...

664
00:41:37,709 --> 00:41:39,336
Underwood.

665
00:41:55,393 --> 00:41:58,760
Doug, LeAnn... do you have a moment?

666
